  <NAME>RNA-sequencing and Exome-sequencing analysis of ferroptosis-resistant 786-O GPX4-null carcinoma cells following in vivo selection</NAME>
  <TITLE>RNA-sequencing and Exome-sequencing analysis of ferroptosis-resistant 786-O GPX4-null carcinoma cells following in vivo selection</TITLE>
  <DESCRIPTION>We have used in vivo selection to isolate GPX4 knockout 786-O cells that have evaded ferroptosis in vivo in mouse xenograft experiments. RNA-seq and Exome-seq profiling were performed to characterize the mechanisms underlying ferroptosis evasion in these in vivo-derived ferroptosis resistant cells. Overall design: Two tumor cell lines were isolated from GPX4 wildtype 786-O tumors. Four GPX4-null 786-O cell lines were isolated from overt GPX4-knockout tumors growing on two mice. Two replicates of each cell line were performed in the RNA-Seq experiment. One replicate of each cell line was performed in the Exome-seq experiment. WTL: (GPX4) wildtype, left tumor WTR: (GPX4) wildtype, right tumor FR2aL: Secondary ferroptosis-resistant line from mouse1 (a), left tumor FR2aR: Secondary ferroptosis-resistant line from mouse1 (a), right tumor FR2dL: Secondary ferroptosis-resistant line from mouse2 (or "d"), left tumor FR2dR: Secondary ferroptosis-resistant line from mouse2 (or "d"), right tumor</DESCRIPTION>
